BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) Information Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T120000
UID:6a5e99f388e9bf2800322b5c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Drop in for the information session on\nSat
 urday\, October 17\, 2026\, 10 am-12 pm\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery S
 aturday\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, October 24 - December 12\, 2026\, 10
  am-1 pm\n. Registration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto t
 ickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all par
 ticipants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis progr
 am is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. G
 erstein Crisis Centre is solely responsible for the protection of \nperson
 al information collected through the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Children's Program Room - Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e99f388e9bf2800322b5c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T193000
UID:6a495489541102b7fa8a674a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Riverdale branch and its neighbourhood is home to a vari
 ety of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore the
  natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize diffe
 rent species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.
 \nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nThe tour w
 ill start and end at the Riverdale Branch and will be guided by the City 
 of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces al
 ong the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor progr
 am (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). T
 his program takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement we
 ather\, registrants will be notified of an alternative date.\nThis program
  is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Frien
 ds of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\
 n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a495489541102b7fa8a674a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
