BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Revitalizing Biodiversity in a Toronto Ravine on Public and Privat
 e Land – The Nordheimer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T190000
UID:6a557a85e9de6536001b836d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this presentation\, environmental researcher Susan Aaron wi
 ll explore the following questions: What is a ravine--historically and tod
 ay--as a base for natural revitalization and water retention and human and
  wildlife use? How do ravines reinvent what a city is\, as having a natura
 l base rather than a concrete one? And how might ravines inform us of the 
 linkages across public and private land\, informing both biodiversity and
  sustainability?
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a557a85e9de6536001b836d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
